<title>POLAND: POLAND'S BANK ZACHODNI SELLS WALBRZYCH MUNIBONDS.</title>
<headline>POLAND'S BANK ZACHODNI SELLS WALBRZYCH MUNIBONDS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Zachodni SA on Monday started to sell in secondary trade the 20 milllion zloty municipal bond issue of city of Walbrzych, it said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the three year munibonds have a coupon of 52-week T-bill plus 80 basis points.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
